        "committer": {
          "name": "Chris Horn",
          "email": "chorn@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-06-26 17:47:13.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20290 lnet: group discovery views by a pluggable source",
        "message": "LU-20290 lnet: group discovery views by a pluggable source\n\nThe self-only discovery-view policy advertised exactly one NID per\nview, so a client saw each server NIC as its own single-NID peer. A\nNUMA-aligned pair of NICs that should be coalesced into one multi-rail\npeer cannot be expressed that way.\n\nGeneralize the single active policy into a group policy: it advertises\none view per group of local NIDs, keyed on the ingress NI, so a client\ncoalesces each group into one multi-rail peer. Where the groups come\nfrom is a pluggable group source below the policy -- the only thing\nthat varies between groupings. This commit ships the per-ni source,\nwhich makes each NI its own singleton group and is therefore\nbyte-identical to the self-only policy it replaces.\n\nGroup membership lives in a refcounted per-generation table reached\nthrough a new pb_group_table pointer on the ping buffer. A view\nresolves its group only through its own buffer's table, so current and\nretiring generations coexist across a make-before-break refresh and\neach table is freed when its last referencing buffer is freed. The\nattach path stamps the table and key before the policy, so any view\nreachable on the serve path -- which gates on a non-NULL policy --\nalready has its backing table.\n\nlnet_self_nets is retained as the participating-net list and selects\nthe per-ni source. The self-only selectors and vtable are removed; the\nnet-list parsing front-end is kept.\n\nNo functional change: a per-ni group is a single NID, so view content,\nserve, and push behave exactly as the self-only policy did.\n\nTest-Parameters: forbuildonly\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I8f7dc5163b8f1d9fb46a970c64af512322b3c1fa\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
